            <ArticleTitle>Fracture of coronary artery sirolimus eluting stent with formation of four aneurysms.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S125-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.2459/JCM.0b013e32833dae07</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary stent fracture is a relatively rare but potentially serious complication of coronary artery stenting, in particular with sirolimus-eluting stents. It has been recognized as one possible cause of in-stent restenosis as well as acute stent thrombosis. The formation of coronary artery aneurysm is one of the critical complications after percutaneous coronary intervention and it has been described after a stent fracture too. We report here a case of formation of four coronary artery aneurysms associated with the fracture of a sirolimus-eluting stent.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
